. LESSON 7 DEVICE VARIABLES AND PORTS
. In these examples color 1 is teal, not red. $L1 says which of the
. palette's 256 colors color 1 shows (lesson 7); 29 is teal, and
. $L1=1 makes it red again.
$L1=29
. In fullscreen the keyboard and mouse are joystick 1: the arrow keys
. push the stick, $X1 and $Y1, the mouse button is the trigger, $T1, and
. the mouse across the screen is the knob, $K1. ESC leaves fullscreen,
. and the macro carries on; the node's Stop button stops it.
. Type RANGE, DRAW, COLORS, CHOOSY or CLOCK to try them.
RANGE=[PRINT $T1;SKIP 0]

DRAW=[IF $T1==1,POINT X=X+$X1,Y=Y+$Y1,3
SKIP -1]

DRAW=[POINT X=X+$X1,Y=Y+$Y1,3
IF $T1==0,POINT X,Y,0
SKIP -2]

DRAW=[K=0
X=X+$X1;Y=Y+$Y1
   BOX X,Y,1,20,5
   BOX X,Y,20,1,5
IF (K=K+1)\2==1,SKIP -2
IF $T1==1,BOX X,Y,3,3,$K1/64+2
SKIP -5]

PRINT $L0,$L1,$L2,$L3

COLORS=[$L0=$L0+$X1;SKIP 0]

CHOOSY=[PRINT "MOVE THE KNOB SIDE TO SIDE
   TO CHANGE COLOR
AND TURN IT TO CHANGE BRIGHTNESS
PULL TRIGGER TO PRINT VALUE"
A=0
   A=A+$X1*8;IF A<0,A=0
   IF A>248,A=248
   $L0=A+$K1/32+4
IF $T1==1,PRINT $L0
SKIP -4]

. $HB is where the right half colors $R0-$R3 start, in 8 pixel columns.
CBARS=[CL;A=-149;C=0;$HB=21
$R0=0;$R1=82;$R2=43;$R3=249
$L0=7;$L1=213;$L2=126;$L3=164
IF A<115,BOX A=A+45,0,46,202,C=(C+1)\3+1;SKIP 0]

CLOCK=[PRINT "INPUT HOUR,MINUTE,SECOND"
INPUT $HR,$MN,$SC
PRINT $HR,$MN,$SC;SKIP 0]

. THE ANIMATION. CBARS draws six bars, three in the left colors and three
. in the right. MARQUEE then hands each color on to the next slot,
. $L1 to $L3 and $R1 to $R3, so the colors march along the bars. Only
. the colors change, never the picture, so there is nothing to redraw.
. The node's Stop button stops it, and Play carries on.
CBARS
MARQUEE=[A=$L1;$L1=$L2;$L2=$L3;$L3=A
A=$R1;$R1=$R2;$R2=$R3;$R3=A;WAIT 8;SKIP -1]
MARQUEE
